.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-logs 1  "ngx-logs " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-logs \- Show a site\*(Aqs access log (or error log with \-e)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-logs\fR [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-error\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-follow\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISITE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show a site\*(Aqs access log (or error log with \-e)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-error\fR
Error log instead of access log
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-follow\fR
Keep following new lines (Ctrl\-C to stop)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-lines\fR \fI<LINES>\fR [default: 50]
Number of lines to show
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISITE\fR>
Site ID (from `ngx ls`) or any of its domain names
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  ngx logs 4 \-f
  ngx logs 4 \-e \-n 200
